azelcast-3.4.0.json`\\n\\n1. Decide whether this library should be handled as Hazelcast `3.4` rather than `3.4.0`, and update the version/tag mapping accordingly.\\n2. Populate valid source, test, and documentation URLs for the chosen version or upstream tag, then regenerate the test project.\\n3. Rerun the library workflow once generation succeeds so tests and dynamic-access metrics can be produced.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":161275,\"cached_input_tokens\":109696,\"output_tokens\":4671,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":2457}}\n--- preflight decision record ---\n19:    \"action\": \"no_action\" | \"advisory_preparation\",\n20:    \"summary\": \"short reason\",\n23:    \"risks\": [\"risk notes, if any\"]\n2501:[assistant]   \"action\": \"no_action\",\n2502:[assistant]   \"summary\": \"Hazelcast 3.4 is an embeddable library that can provide meaningful map and serialization coverage in-process without Docker, extra dependencies, or environment configuration.\",\n2505:[assistant]   \"risks\": [\n2514:[recv] agent_end\n--- target discovery output ---\n{\n  \"coordinates\" : \"com.hazelcast:hazelcast:3.4.0\"\n}\n--- branch latest commit ---\neb34ff622d747c495dddb92fd63829f5c6121c72\nPreserve failed automation work for issue #515\n\n--- searched test generation commands / results ---\n3:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Using the `review-library-new-request` skill because this is a `library-new-request` failure triage task. I’m starting by reading the skill guidance and the available run artifacts so I can identify the failing stage and draft the exact issue comment without changing anything.\"}}\n5:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,220p' skills/review-library-new-request/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"---\\nname: review-library-new-request\\ndescription: Review pull requests with t